<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>vpn-password reset</title>
  <style>
    body { color:#202124;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.55;margin:32px;max-width:900px; }
    h1, h2 { color:#1f2933; }
    h1 { border-bottom:2px solid #d8dee4;padding-bottom:8px; }
    li { margin:6px 0; }
    table { border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0; }
    th, td { border:1px solid #999;padding:8px;text-align:left; }
    th { background:#f1f5f9; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>VPN Password Reset Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)</h1>
<p>This SOP outlines the steps for resetting VPN passwords, ensuring a secure and efficient process.</p>

<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p>The purpose of this SOP is to provide a standardized procedure for resetting VPN passwords, ensuring that all necessary steps are taken to minimize disruptions and ensure security.</p>

<h2>Scope</h2>
<ol>
  <li>The scope of this SOP includes resetting VPN passwords for authorized personnel only.</li>
  <li>The SOP applies to all employees with access to the company's VPN system.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The employee has a valid reason for requesting a password reset (e.g., forgotten password, hardware failure).</li>
  <li>The employee has obtained necessary documentation and approvals (if required).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Roles and Responsibilities</h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0">
  <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr><td>IT Administrator</td><td>Manage VPN passwords, perform resets as needed.</td></tr></tbody>
  <tbody><tr><td>Employee Requesting Password Reset</td><td>Obtain necessary documentation and approvals, notify IT Administrator of password reset request.</td></tr></tbody>
</table>

<h2>Procedure</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Step 1: Request a VPN Password Reset</li>
  <li>Step 2: Obtain Necessary Documentation and Approvals (if required)</li>
  <li>Step 3: Notify IT Administrator of Password Reset Request</li>
  <li>Step 4: Wait for IT Administrator to Process Password Reset</li>
  <li>Step 5: Verify New VPN Password and Test Connectivity</li>
</ol>

<h2>Required Screenshot / Image</h2>
<div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:16px;background:#f5f5f5;">
  <strong>Image Placeholder:</strong> The generated image will be inserted here after ServiceNow attachment upload.
</div>

<h2>Validation</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Verify that the new VPN password is correctly entered and functional.</li>
  <li>Test connectivity to ensure VPN access is restored.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0">
  <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Resolution</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr>
    <td>VPN connection fails after password reset.</td>
    <td>Cause: Incorrect or non-existent VPN credentials.</td>
    <td>Resolution: Verify that the new VPN password is correctly entered and functional, or contact IT Administrator for assistance.</td>
  </tr></tbody>
  <tbody><tr>
    <td>Password reset fails due to system issue.</td>
    <td>Cause: System downtime, network connectivity issues, etc.</td>
    <td>Resolution: Wait for system administrator to resolve the issue or contact IT Administrator for assistance.</td>
  </tr></tbody>
</table>

<h2>Rollback / Recovery</h2>
<ol>
  <li>In case of a failed password reset, wait for IT Administrator's guidance before attempting another attempt.</li>
  <li>Follow established recovery procedures to restore previous VPN credentials (if applicable).</li>
</ol>

<h2>References</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The company's VPN system documentation and policies.</li>
  <li>The ServiceNow password reset process.</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
